      "content_html": "<p style=\"margin:0 0 0.75em;padding:5px 10px;background:#f0f4f8;border-left:3px solid #7b9fc4;border-radius:3px;font-size:0.82em;color:#444;line-height:1.8;\">🌲 🏔️ 🔭 <a href=\"https://zirnhelt.github.io/super-rss-feed/review.html?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.sciencealert.com%2Fas-permafrost-melts-toxic-metals-are-poisoning-rivers-with-levels-70-times-higher-than-normal\" style=\"color:#7b9fc4;text-decoration:none;\">✏️</a></p>\n<figure><img alt=\"As Permafrost Melts, Toxic Metals Are Poisoning Rivers With Levels 70 Times Higher Than Normal\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" height=\"1440\" src=\"https://www.sciencealert.com/images/2026/09/Kutuk_2016_2-2560x1440-1.jpg\" width=\"2560\"/><figcaption>An aerial view of the Kutuk River in Alaska's Gates of the Arctic National Park. (Ken Hill/National Park Service)</figcaption></figure>\n<p><img alt=\"As Permafrost Melts, Toxic Metals Are Poisoning Rivers With Levels 70 Times Higher Than Normal\" class=\"attachment-large size-large wp-post-image\" height=\"675\" src=\"https://www.sciencealert.com/images/2026/09/Kutuk_2016_2-2560x1440-1-1200x675.jpg\" style=\"float:left;margin:0 15px 15px 0;\" width=\"1200\"/>An unexpected side effect of a thawing world.</p><p><a href=\"https://www.sciencealert.com/newsletter?utm_source=rss_feed&amp;utm_medium=feed&amp;utm_campaign=rss_feed_promo\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">ScienceAlert stories are written, fact-checked, and edited by humans, never generated by AI. Don't miss a story, subscribe here.</a></p>",
